1434
01:26:03,571 --> 01:26:07,181
The subtle art of scaring away Pakistani men from a second date.

1435
01:26:07,261 --> 01:26:09,255
Assalam o alikum, Junaid Bhai.

1436
01:26:09,335 --> 01:26:11,842
This is ABC writing from Nuremberg, Germany.

1437
01:26:11,922 --> 01:26:17,160
I'm twenty-seven, well settled, working independent and honestly emotionally exhausted.

1438
01:26:17,240 --> 01:26:28,240
I've reached a point where I'm starting to wonder if the problem really is me or if I'm simply living in a society where a woman knowing what she wants is treated as arrogance.

1439
01:26:28,520 --> 01:26:29,290
Here's my story.

1440
01:26:29,370 --> 01:26:33,725
Every time I start talking to someone, usually a fellow Pakistani abroad,

1441
01:26:33,805 --> 01:26:35,717
I make my stance clear from day one.

1442
01:26:35,797 --> 01:26:38,239
I won't be living with in-laws after marriage.

1443
01:26:38,319 --> 01:26:41,160
That one sentence is enough to end the conversation.

1444
01:26:41,240 --> 01:26:45,220
You can almost feel the disappointment through the screen like I just announced I'm applying for.

1445
01:26:45,300 --> 01:26:46,242
for asylum in hell.

1446
01:26:46,322 --> 01:26:49,120
Even when I dated an Indian Muslim guy from Udaipur,

1447
01:26:49,200 --> 01:26:51,539
I thought maybe things would be different.

1448
01:26:51,619 --> 01:26:54,139
But even for him, this was a deal breaker.

1449
01:26:54,219 --> 01:26:55,322
That's when it hit me.

1450
01:26:55,402 --> 01:26:56,855
It's not about nationality.

1451
01:26:56,935 --> 01:26:58,226
It's about conditioning.

1452
01:26:58,306 --> 01:27:00,189
We've all been fed the same script.

1453
01:27:00,269 --> 01:27:01,318
A good woman adjusts,

1454
01:27:01,398 --> 01:27:07,100
sacrifices and quietly merges her identity into her husband's family like a drop of water in the ocean.

1455
01:27:07,180 --> 01:27:11,900
Before people start typing Kaleshi, Family Todnewali and all the creative in the world.

1456
01:27:11,980 --> 01:27:13,933
insults in your comment section.

1457
01:27:14,013 --> 01:27:14,910
Let me say this.

1458
01:27:14,990 --> 01:27:16,637
I've seen my mother's life.

1459
01:27:16,717 --> 01:27:21,253
She was an educated woman working as a clerk independent before marriage.

1460
01:27:21,333 --> 01:27:26,980
But right after it, she was told to quit her job and take up the more important work,

1461
01:27:27,060 --> 01:27:30,356
cooking, cleaning and serving everyone except herself.

1462
01:27:30,436 --> 01:27:35,136
Watching her slowly fade behind her smile is what shaped my boundaries today.

1463
01:27:35,216 --> 01:27:37,600
I've been on dates with nine different men.

1464
01:27:37,680 --> 01:27:44,260
this past year, serious ones, not casual time-pass conversations, and almost every single one had the same script.

1465
01:27:44,340 --> 01:27:50,680
Of course I love you, but my parents will live with us. The more honest ones at least said it upfront.

1466
01:27:51,080 --> 01:27:55,392
The rest wrapped in sweet words like, haan dekh lenge, we'll figure it out together.

1467
01:27:55,472 --> 01:27:56,961
We both know what that means.

1468
01:27:57,041 --> 01:28:01,440
I'll be the one figuring it out while he stands silently on the sidelines.

1469
01:28:01,520 --> 01:28:04,300
So here I am, Junaid, asking you sincerely, am I being un-

1470
01:28:04,380 --> 01:28:09,620
being unreasonable or am I being just human? Someone who's worked hard for her life knows

1471
01:28:09,700 --> 01:28:15,220
what she wants and refuses to step into the same emotional trap she saw her mother stuck in.

1472
01:28:15,300 --> 01:28:18,586
You've always spoken up about women's rights and mental health.

1473
01:28:18,666 --> 01:28:23,711
That's one of the reasons I respect you so deeply because in our so-called progressive Pakistan,

1474
01:28:23,791 --> 01:28:25,877
