2954
03:04:13,565 --> 03:04:16,350
Learn to follow them and be very mindful.

2955
03:04:17,590 --> 03:04:19,510
You will be able to move without any problem.

2956
03:04:19,590 --> 03:04:21,510
No battery will go into the luggage.

2957
03:04:21,590 --> 03:04:23,510
Do you understand?

2958
03:04:23,590 --> 03:04:25,510
Keep in mind.

2959
03:04:25,590 --> 03:04:27,510
Because of you, 300-400 people can die.

2960
03:04:27,590 --> 03:04:29,510
Okay, they are in the luggage.

2961
03:04:29,590 --> 03:04:31,510
I tried to move but I couldn't.

2962
03:04:31,590 --> 03:04:33,510
My left shoulder was completely torn apart.

2963
03:04:33,590 --> 03:04:35,510
And my arm wasn't moving at all.

2964
03:04:35,590 --> 03:04:37,510
It was still attached.

2965
03:04:37,590 --> 03:04:39,510
But deep down I knew something was terribly wrong.

2966
03:04:39,590 --> 03:04:41,510
I could feel warm blood pouring out.

2967
03:04:41,590 --> 03:04:45,340
And the pain was beyond anything I could ever describe.

2968
03:04:45,540 --> 03:04:50,300
God. I screamed for help as people climbed over me to get out. Oh God.

2969
03:04:50,380 --> 03:04:50,680
Oh.

2970
03:04:50,760 --> 03:04:55,372
Now obviously everyone is worried about their lives so they won't think about who is down there,

2971
03:04:55,452 --> 03:04:56,721
whose hand is cut or what.

2972
03:04:56,801 --> 03:04:58,460
People are jumping on top of that.

2973
03:04:58,540 --> 03:05:05,460
I screamed for help. I started suffocating under the weight of bags trying to breathe and call out.

2974
03:05:05,540 --> 03:05:10,540
Eventually people came together and lifted the bus because my arm was stuck and oh.

2975
03:05:13,900 --> 03:05:16,580
Under it, when I pulled out my bleeding heavily.

2976
03:05:17,660 --> 03:05:19,300
When I.

2977
03:05:20,420 --> 03:05:22,755
I was pulled out bleeding heavily by Allah's mercy,

2978
03:05:22,835 --> 03:05:24,849
a doctor who happened to be on the motorway,

2979
03:05:24,929 --> 03:05:28,660
stopped and gave me first aid until the motorway police and ambulance arrived.

2980
03:05:29,180 --> 03:05:33,020
They took me first to Shekupura DHQ Hospital, but there was little help.

2981
03:05:33,700 --> 03:05:34,380
Over there.

2982
03:05:34,660 --> 03:05:36,700
From there I was moved to Jinnah Hospital, Lahore.

2983
03:05:36,780 --> 03:05:37,700
Oh God.

2984
03:05:38,500 --> 03:05:41,060
Where is Jinnah Hospital? Where is the motorway?

2985
03:05:42,400 --> 03:05:44,600
Oh, God.

2986
03:05:46,600 --> 03:05:49,600
But again the staff's attitude was careless and arrogant.

2987
03:05:50,790 --> 03:05:53,942
My parents had reached by then and seeing the situation,

2988
03:05:54,022 --> 03:05:56,837
my aunt's husband who had connections in the army,

2989
03:05:56,917 --> 03:05:59,520
arranged for me to be admitted to CMH Lahore.

2990
03:05:59,600 --> 03:06:04,600
That's why in the family, one is a soldier, one is a lawyer, one is a policeman, one is a bureaucrat.

2991
03:06:04,870 --> 03:06:05,986
Make this synergy.

2992
03:06:06,066 --> 03:06:12,600
Those who have four children, Amar Akbar Anthony and Cynthia, whatever, do this.

2993
03:06:12,940 --> 03:06:18,860
This is the motto, this is the key to success in this country.

2994
03:06:18,940 --> 03:06:20,860
Anyways, CMH went to Lahore.

2995
03:06:20,940 --> 03:06:25,860
That's where I ended up spending the next three years of, oh God, three years.

2996
03:06:25,940 --> 03:06:30,860
My left arm was completely destroyed. The muscles, tendons and tissue were gone.

2997
03:06:30,940 --> 03:06:35,860
The doctors and parents decided to do everything possible to save it from amputation.

2998
03:06:35,940 --> 03:06:39,940
And that began a long, painful journey filled with surgeries, complications.

2999
03:06:40,230 --> 03:06:43,022
complications and endless procedures.

3000
03:06:43,102 --> 03:06:46,342
Over the next few years, I underwent countless surgeries.

3001
03:06:46,422 --> 03:06:48,030
There were skin grafts taken.

3002
03:06:48,510 --> 03:06:50,430
Twice from my legs.

3003
03:06:50,510 --> 03:06:54,430
Oh, the skin is removed from here and applied here.

3004
03:06:54,510 --> 03:06:56,430
Oh God.

3005
03:06:56,510 --> 03:06:58,510
By the way, think about it.

3006
03:06:58,650 --> 03:07:00,570
Extra skin in the thigh.

3007
03:07:00,650 --> 03:07:03,570
Of course, knowing that they will be doing this in the future.

3008
03:07:03,650 --> 03:07:05,650
This is where the savings are made.

3009
03:07:05,770 --> 03:07:11,210
And even I had a flap surgery where my arm was stitched to my stomach for two months.

3010
03:07:14,040 --> 03:07:16,620
Okay, what's that?

3011
03:07:18,040 --> 03:07:22,600
My stomach was literally cut open so that my arm could be inserted inside a la-

3012
03:07:22,680 --> 03:07:24,180
Okay.

3013
03:07:24,720 --> 03:07:28,560
Cut the arm and put it inside the stomach.

3014
03:07:29,220 --> 03:07:31,900
So that natural tissue formation happens from there.

3015
03:07:32,240 --> 03:07:33,280
Dude, this also happens?

3016
03:07:33,360 --> 03:07:34,740
Oh God, God, God, God.

3017
03:07:34,820 --> 03:07:35,620
May God have mercy.

3018
03:07:35,700 --> 03:07:38,580
Dude, just think how much medical science has progressed.

3019
03:07:38,660 --> 03:07:39,860
How much has it progressed.

3020
03:07:40,530 --> 03:07:41,730
where to save it.

3021
03:07:45,230 --> 03:07:47,630
and hardest experiences of my life.

3022
03:07:47,920 --> 03:07:51,922
I regained some circulation in my fingers, but not enough to function.

3023
03:07:52,002 --> 03:07:54,885
Despite all the operations, infection started spreading.

3024
03:07:54,965 --> 03:07:58,018
My body grew weaker and I had several near-death experiences.

3025
03:07:58,098 --> 03:08:00,450
Once due to severe shivering.

3026
03:08:01,220 --> 03:08:07,580
weakness. My body almost gave up. Another time my hemoglobin dropped to 4.3 which is life-threatening.

3027
03:08:07,660 --> 03:08:11,580
Through all of it, I kept praying I had always been somewhere.

3028
03:08:11,660 --> 03:08:18,580
Someone with trust, complete trust in Allah and I realized that this was my biggest test.

3029
03:08:18,660 --> 03:08:24,580
After two years and eight months of trying everything, the infection worsened.

3030
03:08:24,660 --> 03:08:31,580
My health was deteriorating badly and the doctors finally told us that amputation was the only way to save my life.

3031
03:08:31,660 --> 03:08:35,660
Chahar teen saal they really tried. The decision broke me.

3032
03:08:35,910 --> 03:08:39,694
But I had already seen so much pain that I quietly accepted it.

3033
03:08:39,774 --> 03:08:44,911
When I woke up after the surgery, looked down, realizing that my arm was gone forever.

3034
03:08:44,991 --> 03:08:47,520
It felt like my entire world had collapsed.

3035
03:08:47,600 --> 03:08:50,055
I won't go into every medical detail.

3036
03:08:50,135 --> 03:08:51,311
It would take pages.

3037
03:08:51,391 --> 03:08:56,293
But I can tell you this, Junaid Bhai, during the years my classmates were sitting,

3038
03:08:56,373 --> 03:08:58,784
starting college and living normal lives.

3039
03:08:58,864 --> 03:09:01,296
I was in the hospital fighting for mine.

3040
03:09:01,376 --> 03:09:03,290
I spent my birthdays under anesthesia.

3041
03:09:03,370 --> 03:09:09,290
My wounds were scrubbed raw every day and my cries echoed through the hospital wards.

3042
03:09:09,370 --> 03:09:14,290
Through it all, I had no friends visiting, no relatives who truly stood by me.

3043
03:09:14,370 --> 03:09:19,290
Just my mother. My father was working in Dubai and he came only for major surgeries.

3044
03:09:19,370 --> 03:09:22,290
But it was my mom who stayed beside me every single day.

3045
03:09:22,370 --> 03:09:26,290
She was my nurse, my motivator and my emotional shield.

3046
03:09:26,370 --> 03:09:29,290
She never let me see her break down.

3047
03:09:29,370 --> 03:09:31,210
She would scold me like but…

3048
03:09:31,290 --> 03:09:36,410
Like, stop it, get better soon, I can't babysit you forever.

3049
03:09:36,490 --> 03:09:38,810
Just to make me laugh and push me to stay strong.

3050
03:09:38,890 --> 03:09:43,190
Now that I am older, I realize how much emotional strength it took for her to hide

3051
03:09:43,270 --> 03:09:45,490
her pain and keep me hopeful.

3052
03:09:45,570 --> 03:09:48,370
My doctor and my mother are the reason I am still alive today.

3053
03:09:48,450 --> 03:09:52,210
I will never forget how they kept me going when I was ready to give up.

3054
03:09:52,290 --> 03:09:55,690
And when the amputation finally happened, I made a promise to myself that I would

3055
03:09:55,770 --> 03:09:57,690
never let this disability define me.

3056
03:09:58,180 --> 03:10:02,500
I would rebuild my life not through sympathy but through skill, creativity and hard work.

3057
03:10:02,580 --> 03:10:06,940
I still remember one of my major surgeries when I was seventeen.

3058
03:10:07,020 --> 03:10:12,740
Instead of a birthday cake, the doctors were cutting open my stomach for a flap procedure and my doctor joked,

3059
03:10:12,820 --> 03:10:14,940
here's your cake today.

3060
03:10:15,020 --> 03:10:16,420
Oh fuck man.

3061
03:10:16,500 --> 03:10:19,420
We laughed because that's all we could do.

3062
03:10:19,500 --> 03:10:25,380
Those small moments of humor, okay, you found it funny, okay.

3063
03:10:26,180 --> 03:10:33,700
Those small moments of humor and hope are what got me through the darkest days.

3064
03:10:33,780 --> 03:10:39,060
I saw the real faces of people during those years who stood by us and who didn't.

3065
03:10:39,140 --> 03:10:43,140
My mother was alone most of the time, fighting both emotionally and financially.

3066
03:10:43,220 --> 03:10:48,660
When COVID hit, I was finally discharged through my, though my body was still healing,

3067
03:10:48,740 --> 03:10:52,660
my stomach, legs, and shoulders all had graft scars.

3068
03:10:52,860 --> 03:10:55,565
I still needed daily dressings but I didn't stop.

3069
03:10:55,645 --> 03:10:59,920
I went back to studying, determined to finish my O levels and then A levels.

3070
03:11:00,000 --> 03:11:02,913
Over time, Alhamdulillah, my body began to heal.

3071
03:11:02,993 --> 03:11:05,767
The wounds closed, but the scars remained deep,

3072
03:11:05,847 --> 03:11:08,680
permanent marks that told the story of survival.

3073
03:11:08,760 --> 03:11:10,854
Even after I was physically stable,

3074
03:11:10,934 --> 03:11:16,560
I started facing something I hadn't experienced before, PTSD and intense phantom pain.

3075
03:11:16,640 --> 03:11:19,960
It was like my mind and body were still stuck in an accident.

3076
03:11:20,040 --> 03:11:24,500
Some nights I could feel my missing arm hurting as if it were still there.

3077
03:11:24,580 --> 03:11:27,840
The pain was so real it would wake me up.

3078
03:11:27,920 --> 03:11:34,720
I'd look at my shoulder confused, unable to make sense of how my body could remember something that no longer existed.

3079
03:11:34,800 --> 03:11:40,880
I also struggled mentally. Hospitals, loud noises, and even the sound of sirens would trigger flashbacks.

3080
03:11:40,960 --> 03:11:46,182
I had seen so much in those years, blood, surgeries, near-death moments,

3081
03:11:46,262 --> 03:11:48,000
that it left a lasting imprint.

3082
03:11:48,080 --> 03:11:54,480
on my mind. I tried to stay strong but there were days when the memories became too heavy.

3083
03:11:54,560 --> 03:11:57,285
Sorry, I can't read properly because I'm teary.

3084
03:11:57,365 --> 03:12:01,329
That's when I decided to travel to Murree with a few close friends,

3085
03:12:01,409 --> 03:12:03,692
not just for fun but to breathe again,

3086
03:12:03,772 --> 03:12:07,505
to feel alive after so many years of hospitals and quiet rooms.

3087
03:12:07,585 --> 03:12:09,592
I took my Sony A6300 camera with me,

3088
03:12:09,672 --> 03:12:13,920
hoping to reconnect with the one thing that always gave me peace.

3089
03:12:14,460 --> 03:12:20,840
On that trip, I started making a series of short reels, mixing cinematic visuals, and with poetry I wrote myself.

3090
03:12:21,140 --> 03:12:24,695
Each reel was personal about pain, healing, loss, and resilience.

3091
03:12:24,775 --> 03:12:28,437
I didn't expect much, but when I started posting them on Instagram,

3092
03:12:28,517 --> 03:12:29,800
people connected deeply.

3093
03:12:29,880 --> 03:12:32,311
The reels slowly began to gain traction.

3094
03:12:32,391 --> 03:12:35,753
One after another, they started getting shared widely.

3095
03:12:35,833 --> 03:12:41,080
People from all over began to message me saying they felt what I was trying to express.

3096
03:12:41,160 --> 03:12:45,720
Within a year and a half, my Instagram grew to 100K organic followers.

3097
03:12:45,800 --> 03:12:49,080
Those videos weren't just content, they were my therapy.

3098
03:12:49,160 --> 03:12:53,080
Every edit, every line of poetry helped me process what I had been through,

3099
03:12:53,160 --> 03:12:58,600
and reminded me even though I had lost an arm, I hadn't lost my ability to create something meaningful.

3100
03:12:58,680 --> 03:13:04,120
My father saw how passionate I was and decided to support my dream of studying filmmaking.

3101
03:13:04,200 --> 03:13:06,920
I got accepted into SAE Australia.

3102
03:13:07,180 --> 03:13:10,242
Dubai campus, one of the top practical film schools.

3103
03:13:10,322 --> 03:13:15,673
It was expensive, but my father never let money stand between me and my dreams.

3104
03:13:15,753 --> 03:13:21,057
Around the same time, he also brought my mother and younger brother to Dubai,

3105
03:13:21,137 --> 03:13:24,022
and for a while life finally felt peaceful again.

3106
03:13:24,102 --> 03:13:27,185
I continued to grow my Instagram to 150K followers,

3107
03:13:27,265 --> 03:13:32,720
earning through freelance video editing, photo retouching and color grading.

3108
03:13:32,800 --> 03:13:38,560
Worked for weddings, agencies and YouTubers. Everything was stable until another storm hit.

3109
03:13:38,640 --> 03:13:41,939
My father who had always struggled with high blood pressure,

3110
03:13:42,019 --> 03:13:44,000
suddenly complained of severe chest pain.

3111
03:13:44,080 --> 03:13:47,462
It turned out to be an aortic dissection of a leak in his main artery.

3112
03:13:47,542 --> 03:13:51,760
It was a life-threatening situation, but Alhamdulillah survived after major surgery.

3113
03:13:51,840 --> 03:13:54,898
Still, it was a huge financial and emotional setback for our family.

3114
03:13:54,978 --> 03:13:59,080
Even though my father told me not to quit university, I couldn't watch him struggle again.

3115
03:13:59,240 --> 03:14:03,760
He had already sacrificed everything for my treatment and I couldn't let him carry another burden.

3116
03:14:03,840 --> 03:14:06,260
So I started looking for jobs in Dubai desperately.

3117
03:14:06,340 --> 03:14:10,360
Eventually I got a position as a photographer, videographer for a cricket team.

3118
03:14:10,440 --> 03:14:14,460
The pay was low, but I took it thinking at least I could contribute something.

3119
03:14:14,540 --> 03:14:20,960
I worked day and night shooting, editing, planning, managing social media, everything, but over time they started exploiting me.

3120
03:14:21,040 --> 03:14:23,360
They underpaid me and took advantage of my dedication.

3121
03:14:23,440 --> 03:14:26,000
One day during a match in Abu Dhabi, I met a person who.

3122
03:14:26,080 --> 03:14:27,566
who recognized me from Instagram.

3123
03:14:27,646 --> 03:14:30,287
He told me he followed my work and admired my journey.

3124
03:14:30,367 --> 03:14:32,028
When he learned about my situation,

3125
03:14:32,108 --> 03:14:36,855
he introduced me to international clients and soon I started freelancing independently,

3126
03:14:36,935 --> 03:14:38,800
earning ten times more than I did before.

3127
03:14:38,880 --> 03:14:40,828
Desi unke li kabhi kaam mat karna bhai.

3128
03:14:40,908 --> 03:14:42,344
I'll always explore it to you.

3129
03:14:42,424 --> 03:14:45,713
After that freelance opportunity, I eventually moved back to Dubai,

3130
03:14:45,793 --> 03:14:49,608
hoping to build on that momentum and take the step in my professional journey.

3131
03:14:49,688 --> 03:14:53,360
But ever since I came back, life has felt like it hit a pause button again.

3132
03:14:53,460 --> 03:15:00,100
That sense of direction I once had of constantly moving forward learning and growing has slowly started to fade.

3133
03:15:00,180 --> 03:15:05,060
These days I find myself feeling demotivated and drained.

3134
03:15:05,140 --> 03:15:09,234
Even though I'm still trying every single day to get my life back on track,

3135
03:15:09,314 --> 03:15:12,399
I've been applying to marketing agencies,

3136
03:15:12,479 --> 03:15:14,971
production houses and creative studios across Dubai,

3137
03:15:15,051 --> 03:15:19,550
trying to find a stable position where I could contribute my skills in filmmaking,

3138
03:15:19,630 --> 03:15:20,780
photography and editing.

3139
03:15:20,960 --> 03:15:27,880
But it's been heartbreaking, Junaid Bhai. I've faced rejection after rejection, sometimes without even getting a chance to prove myself.

3140
03:15:27,960 --> 03:15:34,880
There are two reasons I've noticed repeatedly behind these rejections. One is being a Pakistani and the other is being disabled.

3141
03:15:34,960 --> 03:15:37,610
I've always believed in honesty and transparency,

3142
03:15:37,690 --> 03:15:43,880
so before every interview I clearly mentioned that I am an amputee because I never want to hide a part of who I am.

3143
03:15:43,960 --> 03:15:46,960
But that honesty has often worked against me.

3144
03:15:48,730 --> 03:15:50,014
as soon as they find out.

3145
03:15:50,094 --> 03:15:52,999
Many don't even bother to review my portfolio, my reel,

3146
03:15:53,079 --> 03:15:55,185
or the projects I've done over the years.

3147
03:15:55,265 --> 03:15:56,909
The work that speaks for itself.

3148
03:15:56,989 --> 03:15:57,577
And it hurts.

3149
03:15:57,657 --> 03:15:58,244
You know why?

3150
03:15:58,324 --> 03:16:02,212
Because I've spent years rebuilding my life after that incident,

3151
03:16:02,292 --> 03:16:07,150
teaching myself new skills, creating content that connected with people,

3152
03:16:07,230 --> 03:16:10,700
working hard to prove that a disability doesn't define capability.

3153
03:16:10,780 --> 03:16:15,810
But lately it feels like all these efforts are being overlooked as if none of it counts.

3154
03:16:15,890 --> 03:16:19,690
It counts once people see me as different.

3155
03:16:19,770 --> 03:16:24,730
Every day I wake up, open my laptop, send out applications, write personalized messages,

3156
03:16:24,810 --> 03:16:25,850
and try to network.

3157
03:16:25,930 --> 03:16:29,610
But the silence that follows has started to weigh heavy on my heart.

3158
03:16:29,690 --> 03:16:30,360
At this point,

3159
03:16:30,440 --> 03:16:39,810
I find myself emotionally exhausted and I keep questioning whether I'm doing something wrong or whether the world just doesn't want to give people like me a fair chance.

3160
03:16:39,890 --> 03:16:42,630
There are days when I push myself to stay positive, reminding myself of.

3161
03:16:42,710 --> 03:16:44,713
of everything I've survived,

3162
03:16:44,793 --> 03:16:50,630
but there are also days when it feels like I'm slipping back in the dark place of uncertainty.

3163
03:16:50,710 --> 03:16:53,303
The reason I'm writing this email, Junaid Bhai, is not for sympathy.

3164
03:16:53,383 --> 03:16:55,029
It's because after listening to you for years,

3165
03:16:55,109 --> 03:16:57,730
I've developed a deep respect and emotional connection with your words.

3166
03:16:57,810 --> 03:17:01,730
You speak with honesty, compassion and experience, things that are rare to find.

3167
03:17:01,810 --> 03:17:07,030
You've always addressed people's struggles with such clarity and warmth that it gives them hope again.

3168
03:17:07,110 --> 03:17:09,920
And honestly, that's what I need right now.

3169
03:17:10,000 --> 03:17:12,620
now a bit of hope and a bit of direction.

3170
03:17:12,700 --> 03:17:16,947
I consider you like an elder brother, someone whose perspective I truly value.

3171
03:17:17,027 --> 03:17:25,787
I just wanted to put my heart out to you to share what I've been through and where I currently stand to seek your genuine advice on how can I move forward again.

3172
03:17:25,867 --> 03:17:30,474
If there's anything you can say or suggest that could help me realign my path,

3173
03:17:30,554 --> 03:17:32,477
it would truly mean the world to me.

3174
03:17:32,557 --> 03:17:36,870
And before I end this, I just want to say you're doing an amazing work, the kind

3175
03:17:36,950 --> 03:17:39,940
The kind of impact your words have on people,

3176
03:17:40,020 --> 03:17:45,970
the way you use your platform to help others to bring perspective and positivity really matters.

3177
03:17:46,050 --> 03:17:51,690
Please keep doing what you're doing because there are countless people like me who find strength and motivation through your voice.

3178
03:17:51,770 --> 03:17:58,845
I have also attached my portfolio and resume below in case you would like to have a look at the work I've done so far.

3179
03:17:58,925 --> 03:17:59,970
